{
  "title": "std::shared_ptr and weak_ptr: reference counting",
  "chapter": "07-generic-stl",
  "summary": "Slides 176–178: every shared_ptr copy increments a counter in the control block; the object dies when it reaches 0. A weak_ptr observes without owning.",
  "code": "struct Quote { double px; };\n\nint main() {\n  auto p = std::make_shared<Quote>( 101.5 );\n  {\n    auto q = p;                   // shared ownership\n    std::weak_ptr<Quote> w = p;   // observer\n  }\n  std::weak_ptr<Quote> w2 = p;\n  p.reset();                      // last owner gone\n  bool alive = !w2.expired();     // false\n}",
